#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:1
msgid "Debian/Ubuntu versioning in nightly and prerelease binaries"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:3
msgid ""
"Binary packages produced for prerelease and nightly builds have some "
"particularities to establish the priority among them nicely."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:6
msgid ""
"**Prereleases** for version `X.Y.Z` are created as candidates of the stable "
"release of `X.Y.Z` so the stable needs to have precedence over prereleases "
"when both are available through different repositories."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:10
msgid ""
"**Nightlies** for version `X.Y.Z` are snapshots of development code merged "
"on top of a released version `X.Y.Z`. This includes features and/or patches "
"that will be shipped into the next release. Therefore nightlies need to have "
"precedence over stable releases. Another use case for nightlies is to serve "
"as continuous unstable releases when preparing a new version `X.Y.Z`. In "
"this scenario the stable release should have precedence over the nightlies "
"generated before it. To get this precedence, the nightly version uses the "
"trick of setting the version to `{X-1.99.99}` (i.e: if the version to "
"release is `9.0.0`, the nightlies used before the version will use "
"`8.99.99`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:20
msgid "Version schemes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:22
msgid ""
"**Prerelease** versioning scheme: `{upcoming_version}~pre{prerelease_version}"
"`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:24
msgid ""
"`upcoming_version`: upstream version target for current prerelease series (e."
"g., `X.Y.Z`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:25
msgid "`prerelease_version`: prerelease version number in the series"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:27
msgid ""
"**Nightly** uses the following versioning scheme: "
"`{current_released_version}+git{date}+{nightly_revision}r{hash}-"
"{nightly_revision}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:29
msgid ""
"`current_released_version`: will be the latest version released available in "
"the changelog file of the corresponding `*-release` repo. If the nightly is "
"used for an upcoming release (for example, gazebo10 where X is 10) then "
"{X-1}.99.99-1 (gazebo10_9.99.99-1) form will be used until prereleases or "
"final release."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:34
msgid "`date`: timestamp YYYY-MM-DD"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:36
msgid ""
"`hash`: git hash corresponding to code HEAD used in the nightly build.  Used "
"for information proposes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:39
msgid ""
"`nightly_revision`:  revision number to apply to the nightly. It is also "
"used to generate a new nightly using the same date timestamp."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:42
msgid "Versions when mixing stable, prerelease and nightly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:44
msgid ""
"Which version has priority when using prerelease and stable repositories?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:46
#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:56
#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:68
msgid "packageA version: `1.0.0-1` (stable)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:47
msgid "packageA prerelease: `1.0.1~pre1-1` (prerelease)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:48
msgid "packageA prerelease: `1.0.1~pre2-1` (prerelease)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:49
#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:58
msgid "packageA version: `1.0.1-1` (stable)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:51
msgid "Order: `1.0.1-1` > `1.0.1~pre2-1` > `1.0.1~pre1-1` > `1.0.0`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:53
msgid "Which version has priority when using nightly and stable repositories?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:55
msgid "packageA version: `0.99.99+git201501011r2212b5136299-1` (nightly)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:57
msgid "packageA version: `1.0.0-1+git20150303r6912b5136236-1` (nightly)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:60
msgid ""
"Order: `1.0.1-1` > `1.0.0-1+git20150303r6912b5136236-1` > `1.0.0-1` > "
"`0.99.99+git20150101r2212b5136299-1`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:62
msgid ""
"Which version has priority when using nightly, prerelease and stable "
"repositories?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:64
msgid "packageA version: `0.99.99+git20150101r2212b5136299-1` (nightly)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:65
msgid "packageA prerelease: `1.0.0~pre1` (prerelease)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:66
msgid "packageA version: `1.0.0~pre1+git20150101r2212b5136299-1` (nightly)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:67
msgid "packageA prerelease: `1.0.0~pre2-1` (prerelease)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:70
msgid ""
"Order: `1.0.0-1` > `1.0.0~pre2-1` > `1.0.0~pre1+git20150101r2212b5136299-1` "
"> `1.0.0~pre1-1` > `0.99.99+git20150101r2212b5136299-1`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:72
msgid "MacOS versioning in unstable packages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:74
msgid ""
"Some Brew packages have unstable versions, snapshots of software not "
"corresponding to an official release. The version scheme is typically: "
"`{current_released_version}~${osrf_revision}~{date}~{hash}`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../releasing/versioning_pre_nightly.md:76
msgid ""
"`osrf_revision`: correspond to the revision number that identifies the  "
"packaging metadata being used in the Brew formulae."
msgstr ""
